## XLivelessAddon (original)

The launcher/SecuROM bypass, the save/settings path redirects, the WM_ROM message
window, the borderless window handling and the INI layout descend from
[XLivelessAddon](https://github.com/GTAmodding/XLivelessAddon) by the GTAmodding
community, released into the public domain. `source/skip_launcher.ixx`,
`source/skip_launcher_recovered.inc`, `source/rom_window.ixx`,
`source/savegames.ixx` and `source/windowed.ixx` carry a header that attributes
the bodies.

## ZolikaPatch

The recovered signature tables, the SkipLauncher stage split (main, DFA, ROM),
the DFA file-API hooks and the legacy launcher stage are a reimplementation of
the machine-level behaviour of ZolikaPatch 7.65 by Zolika1351. ZolikaPatch shipped
as a compiled ASI without source; no original source is redistributed here.

## GTAIV.EFLC.FusionFix

The borderless-window/focus-loss logic (`source/windowed.ixx`), the
SHGetFolderPath user-data redirect (`source/profile.ixx`), the
`SkipIntro`/`SkipMenu` mechanism (`source/menu.ixx`, `skipintro.ixx`), the
`grcDevice::GetAvailableVideoMemory` VRAM code (`source/vram.ixx`,
`memory.ixx`) and the shared `Event`, `Log`, `Game` and `find_pattern` shapes
(`source/common.ixx`) follow GTAIV.EFLC.FusionFix (`windowed.ixx`,
`userdata.ixx`, `common.ixx`), Copyright (C) ThirteenAG and contributors,
GPL-3.0. The windowed compatibility gates in
`source/config.ixx` follow the same project's approach. The local-directory
options are deliberately **not** gated on FusionFix being present.

## Pinned submodules

The dependencies are pinned upstream submodules under `external/`, never
committed copies; a fresh checkout needs
`git submodule update --init --recursive`. The licence text of each project is
committed inside its own submodule.

| Path | Project | Pin | Licence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `external/injector` | [SandeMC/injector](https://github.com/SandeMC/injector) (fork of LINK/2012's injector) | `c196f900` | zlib |
| `external/injector/safetyhook` | [cursey/safetyhook](https://github.com/cursey/safetyhook) | `f44cc070` | BSL-1.0 |
| `external/injector/minhook` | [TsudaKageyu/minhook](https://github.com/TsudaKageyu/minhook) | `8af6b4ac` | BSD-2-Clause |
| `external/injector/bddisasm` | [bitdefender/bddisasm](https://github.com/bitdefender/bddisasm) | `709fd970` | Apache-2.0 |
| `external/injector/kananlib` | [cursey/kananlib](https://github.com/cursey/kananlib) | `114de171` | BSL-1.0 |
| `external/injector/utility` | `utility` submodule of the injector tree (praydog) | in-tree | MIT |
| `external/injector/zydis` | Zydis amalgamation shipped inside the injector tree | in-tree (`Zydis.c`/`Zydis.h`) | MIT |
| `external/hooking` | [ThirteenAG/Hooking.Patterns](https://github.com/ThirteenAG/Hooking.Patterns) (NTAuthority, CitizenFX) | `460a47bc` | MIT |
| `external/inireader` | [ThirteenAG/IniReader](https://github.com/ThirteenAG/IniReader) | `a0a5973c` | MIT |
| `external/inireader/mINI` | [metayeti/mINI](https://github.com/metayeti/mINI) (Danijel Durakovic) | bundled by the above | MIT |

The injector pin is the owner's fork. Upstream `MakeRET` stores
`pop ? 0xC2 : 0xC3` through a deduced `int` and writes four bytes for both `ret`
forms; the fork stores a `uint8_t` opcode and a `uint16_t` immediate, so
`injector::MakeRET` emits `ret`/`ret N` at their exact width. The tree calls
`injector::MakeRET` directly and keeps no width workaround.

`CMakeLists.txt` compiles safetyhook's `src/*.cpp` and the injector tree's Zydis
amalgamation (`zydis/Zydis.c`) into `xla_safetyhook`, with
`external/injector/include`, `external/injector/safetyhook/include` and
`external/injector/zydis` on the include path. safetyhook at this pin carries its
x86 mid-hook thunk as assembled bytes in `mid_hook.cpp`; its `.asm` files are the
source of that embed, so there is no MASM step and nothing is fetched at build
time.

The pinned `CIniReader` is all-inline; MSVC 19.51's CL.exe crashes when a
function body that instantiates it is imported into another module interface
unit. The tree keeps the reader inside `source/config.ixx` and makes
`config::Load`/`config::Publish` out-of-line, so `source/dllmain.cpp` remains the
only plain TU. The reader is unmodified.

## Game assets

Grand Theft Auto IV and Episodes from Liberty City are property of Rockstar Games
and Take-Two Interactive. This repository ships no game executables, archives,
